# Virtualenv
.venv/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Secrets and local configuration. .env.example is committed; .env is not.
.env
.env.local

# Generated test images — regenerate with: python tools/make_test_card.py
# The two originals are kept so the project is runnable immediately; the
# batch/ copies are just duplicates and would bloat the history.
samples/batch/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Private keys. ohive.pem sits untracked in this directory: without this rule a
# single `git add -A` commits an SSH private key into history permanently, and
# rewriting history is the only way back out. Ignore the whole class, not the
# one filename.
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# Runtime state: the SQLite database and retained card images. Generated, often
# large, and contains extracted personal data (names, phones, emails) that must
# never reach a public repository.
data/

# Real card photographs used for local testing. buisness.jpeg is a photograph
# of an actual person's business card -- their name, employer, phone and email.
# That is personal data under GDPR and the DPDP Act, and a git repository is
# permanent and, here, pushed to GitHub. Synthetic cards for testing come from
# `python tools/make_test_card.py`; real ones stay on the machine that took them.
# Delete this rule and `git add -f buisness.jpeg` if you deliberately want it in.
buisness.jpeg
# Real card photos supplied for benchmarking. Same reasoning: these are
# photographs of actual people's contact details. They live in samples/real/
# (also ignored) and are referenced by the benchmark by path, never committed.
cl*.jpg
IMG_*.jpg
WhatsApp Image*.jpeg
samples/real/
